WEBVTT

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:37.000
But… God

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:45.000
So, the improvement is needed, basically, because in the previous serialization, what is happening that

00:06:45.000 --> 00:06:57.000
The transaction, if multiple node IDs are set, then when we, like, serialize it to the bytes, and then again deserialize it, it only retrieves the

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:01.000
first node account ID, and that can be like

00:07:01.000 --> 00:07:12.000
cause some error if that node is out of service, or some other issue happened to that. And second issue is that,

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:24.000
When we serialize the chunk transaction, mostly what it does, it only serialized the first chunk, so if we have, like, 14 chunks, only the first chunk gets serialized, and that is

00:07:24.000 --> 00:07:38.000
The one that is get executed, and the 13 remaining one are just negligated. So, that is the reason for, like, the improvement

